// The `all` of all.pil on the std's sum bus (LogUp), in STD_MODE_ONE_INSTANCE (plan M34), with the
// std's MAX_CONSTRAINT_DEGREE raised to 6.
//
// Its state machines put ten terms on the bus, and with the std's default degree (3) its sum bus
// (std_sum.pil, piop_gsum_air) groups them in four im_col columns named `im_cluster` and one
// `im_single`, declared in a loop under the same name, whose evaluations the proof would name alike
// (spec A.6), which the setup refuses. With 6 they take one `im_cluster` and one `im_single` (spec
// Annex F.12); with 4 and 5, still two `im_cluster` or more. The degree is set before the air is
// instantiated: the std reads it when it closes the AIR's bus.
require "all.pil"

set_std_mode(STD_MODE_ONE_INSTANCE);
set_max_constraint_degree(6);

airgroup All {
    All(bus_type: PIOP_BUS_SUM);
}
